        <mxCell id="i34__2" value="The selected VLSIT architecture uses a NEW sharer directory, transaction table, probe scheduler and CCU. OpenHW HPDcache is MODIFY in a separate license-preserving copy for MESI state and tagged probes; the pristine upstream clone remains unchanged. PULP Culsans is architecture reference only because its pinned PlanV cache ports do not match the selected OpenHW HPDcache. Status codes: REUSE = unchanged upstream RTL; REUSE* = candidate pending compatibility checks; MODIFY = source adaptation/wrapper; NEW = VLSIT RTL; GENERATED = CSR RTL from the reviewed workbook. The diagram is a document-grounded proposal, not an integrated RTL hierarchy." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontSize=18;fontColor=#000000;spacing=2;" vertex="1" parent="1" vlsit_library_sha256="D1631ACF98A920526B235E8970FEDDC9305EA2F0D6A35C6529CD220D62AFABB6" vlsit_library_entry="0" vlsit_library_cell="2" vlsit_library_instance="i34">
